{"name":"Après-Ski","hex":"#ced5e4","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"après-ski","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Entertainment, nightlife or social events that take place at a ski resort, after the skiing."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or relating to such events."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/apr%C3%A8s-ski"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ski resort","blocks":[{"text":"A ski resort is a resort developed for skiing, snowboarding, and other winter sports. In Europe, most ski resorts are towns or villages in or adjacent to a ski area, a mountainous area with pistes and a ski lift system. In North America, it is more common for ski areas to exist well away from towns, so ski resorts usually are destination resorts, often purpose-built and self-contained, where skiing is the main activity."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Ski_resorts_in_the_world.png/330px-Ski_resorts_in_the_world.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ski_resort","wikidata":"Q130003"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/World_ski_resorts.png/500px-World_ski_resorts.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/World_ski_resorts.png/1280px-World_ski_resorts.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/World_ski_resorts.png/500px-World_ski_resorts.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Map of world ski resorts","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWorld_ski_resorts.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Cable_car_up_a_mountain_in_France.jpg/500px-Cable_car_up_a_mountain_in_France.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&